Vulkan and SPIR-V interface headers and grammar are fetched under build/deps,
with pinned revisions and SHA-256 checksums. Their upstream copyright and
license notices remain in those archives and installed headers. They are
KhronosGroup/Vulkan-Headers v1.3.296 and KhronosGroup/SPIRV-Headers
vulkan-sdk-1.3.296.0, licensed Apache-2.0 or MIT as specified by upstream.

The optional GLSL fixture compiler is KhronosGroup/glslang 15.1.0. It is
built only as a test tool under build/tools; no glslang code is linked into
libzvk. See that source tree's LICENSE.txt for its notices.

The GPU command encoder is ../zgl/lib/virgl.c and its backend dependencies,
under their own licenses. The Mac test transport uses virglrenderer through
../zgl/tests/vhost. A QEMU virgl host also uses virglrenderer. These host-side
dependencies are separate from zvk's Vulkan objects and SPIR-V compiler.
No Mesa Vulkan driver, NIR, or Mesa SPIR-V compiler is used by libzvk.

Optional loader/validation tooling uses KhronosGroup/Vulkan-Loader and
KhronosGroup/Vulkan-ValidationLayers v1.3.296, plus the validation release's
known-good Vulkan-Utility-Libraries, SPIRV-Tools, SPIRV-Headers and robin-hood
hashing dependencies. They remain in build/tools under their upstream
licenses (including Apache-2.0 and MIT notices). No loader, validation layer
or SPIRV-Tools implementation is linked into libzvk. See validation-tools.py
for archive checksums and immutable dependency commits.

The optional native shared SDK distributes the pinned Apache-2.0 Khronos
loader with sic's private zwm surface port (scripts/native-loader.py),
regenerating dispatch tables from its augmented registry. The loader remains
a separate library and is not linked into libzvk. SDL2 2.30.11 is under its
Zlib license; sic's zwm Vulkan port lives in ../zde/ports/sdl2/port.
The isolated host virglrenderer multisample fix is in
../zgl/tests/patches/virglrenderer-multisample.patch; it is test-host tooling,
not an alternate Vulkan implementation.

The SDK includes shared sic musl (upstream COPYRIGHT and sic NOTICE are
packaged), and Zig's compiler runtime archive (Zig's license is packaged
when supplied by the build toolchain). These are runtime dependencies, not
parts of zvk's shader compiler.

The optional official Vulkan CTS and its dependencies are downloaded into
build/cts for host testing, retain their upstream licenses/notices, and are
not linked into the driver or included in the native SDK.

BC1–BC7 texture preparation uses the vendored bcdec block decoder, by Sergii
Kudlai, at commit 80859ed3b7afb1c527a2a99d70c61457bea72d0c. zVk selects
its MIT license; see vendor/bcdec/LICENSE and the retained header notices.
vendor/bcdec/portability.patch fixes char signedness and undefined signed shifts;
source checksums and provenance are in vendor/bcdec/README.md. The SDK includes
bcdec-LICENSE. This decoder does not execute shaders or render frames.
